    intro: "Whatever you do, work heartily, as for the Lord and not for men, knowing that from the Lord you will receive the inheritance as your reward. You are serving the Lord Christ. Paul tells ordinary workers that their daily tasks are service to Christ. God called Bezalel to craftsmanship, Barnabas and Saul to missions, and countless others to farming, teaching, healing and trading. Every believer is called, first to Christ and then to a way of serving him.",
    context: "In Exodus 31, God filled Bezalel with the Spirit, with ability, intelligence and knowledge in all craftsmanship to build the tabernacle. In Acts 13, the church in Antioch, while worshipping and fasting, heard the Spirit say, Set apart for me Barnabas and Saul for the work to which I have called them. In 1 Corinthians 7, Paul says each should remain in the situation in which he was called, while using opportunities for change. Ephesians 2:10 says we are God's workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God prepared beforehand.",
