    apply: "Review your notes and the memory verses. Revise the tests for claims and the main passages. Pray for peace before the examination and thank God for what you have learned. Plan one habit that you will continue after the course.",
    activity: "Run a quick oral review. The teacher reads a clue such as the final standard for testing and learners name the source and a passage. Ask each learner to name one habit they will keep. End with the reading of Hebrews 1:1-2 and a prayer for the examination.",
    takeHome: "Prepare for the examination by reviewing the revision map, the memory verses and your own summary. Rest well the night before. Pray for classmates.",
    prayer: "Thank God for each lesson. Ask for calm minds and clear memory in the examination. Pray that what we have learned will help us to hear and obey.",
    teacher: "Explain how the examination works: time allowed, question types, and when results will be released. Reassure anxious learners and ensure fair conditions for all, including those who need support. If the examination is held on another date, use this session for guided revision.",
    assess: "This unit is the final examination week. The final examination covers Lessons 1 to 24 and is built from the approved question bank following the curriculum blueprint.",
    mcq1: ["Which verse tells us to test everything and hold fast what is good?", ["1 Thessalonians 5:21", "John 3:16", "Genesis 1:1", "Psalm 150:6"], 0, "1 Thessalonians 5:21."],
    mcq2: ["Which verse says all Scripture is breathed out by God?", ["2 Timothy 3:16", "Romans 12:1", "Acts 2:1", "Matthew 28:19"], 0, "2 Timothy 3:16."],
    tf: ["The final examination covers lessons 1 to 24.", true, "It reviews the whole course."],
    sa: ["In a few sentences, explain how a believer can hear God and test what they think they hear.", ["scripture", "spirit", "counsel", "test", "obey", "humble"], "A good answer says God speaks supremely in Christ and Scripture, believers also receive guidance through the Spirit, conscience, counsel and circumstances, all tested by Scripture, fruit and the community, and they respond in humble obedience."],
